  "text": "19 September 1907:  “considerable ice around the edge of the Bay, the bluff had begun to freeze, and even the exposed clay flat was solid”. LSQ & Hoffman return to Keewalik, find mining operations in interior ceased and nothing else to do. (B.AMNH 26, p.90)",
